# This repository's OWN bookkeeping — the very files the skills here create.
#
# They are working notes belonging to whoever maintains this toolkit: which clone is which,
# what the last session changed, what is still open. A clone should get the skills, not one
# maintainer's session log, so they are deliberately never published.
#
# IN YOUR PROJECT THESE FILES ARE THE POINT AND BELONG IN GIT. Do not copy this rule across —
# the whole argument of the README is that this state must outlive a context window, and a
# project that ignores them has bookkeeping only until the next machine.
#
# Kept here rather than in .git/info/exclude, which was the earlier choice: exclude is not
# cloned and not backed up, so the protection existed on exactly one machine and a fresh
# clone plus `git add -A` would publish everything.
SESSION_HANDOFF.md
CHRONICLE.md
docs/
